        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ensign53/{size}/1904_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-02-08T17:34:57.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>So I had a question: New Bedford was one of my absolute favorite games. I'm looking at picking up a copy for my class for when they learn about whaling and the northeastern region.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I know there had been some printing issues with the first batch, so much that even some fixed tiles had been sent out (and that even those had an isue or two). There was also some talk on BGG about there being a second printing in possible development to fix these issues.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Just wondering: has that re-print ever been done, and if so, is there a way to tell \"V 1.1\" boxes from \"V1.0\"? I would love to use this game as a teaching tool, but worry about misprinted tiles and such.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:52:27.413Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
